# Offline pin notes — gpw-xdm-forces

## Policy

CP2K 2026.1 stock `PAIR_POTENTIAL TYPE` is only
`DFTD2|DFTD3|DFTD3(BJ)|DFTD4` — **no** `TYPE XDM`. Canonical density-dependent
XDM oracles are postg / critic2 / QE. Atomiverse ships the **free-atom**
foothold (geometry-only multipole moments + CRC α) with a dual pure-Python
lattice sum + analytic gradient, same energy path as `gpw-xdm-ice`.

## Geometry

Water dimer (Å), same as `gpw-xdm-ice` / `gpw-ts-ice`:

```
O  0.000000  0.000000  0.000000
H  0.758602  0.000000  0.504284
H  0.758602  0.000000 -0.504284
O  3.000000  0.000000  0.000000
H  3.758602  0.000000  0.504284
H  3.758602  0.000000 -0.504284
```

Cell (periodic pin): ABC 12.0 12.0 12.0 Å, PERIODIC XYZ.
Å→Bohr: `1/0.52917720859` (ATV).
Damping: QE NC-PBE a1=0.4283, a2=4.6657338220946531 Bohr (2.4690 Å).
rcut = 50 Å; image shells via ATV `pair_image_counts` (ceil(rcut/L)+1).

## Energy pin (dual pure-Python ≡ ATV tables)

- Isolated: E_disp = −2.1020435998516220×10⁻³ Ha
- Periodic: E_disp = −2.1148157612879029×10⁻³ Ha

## Force dual-gate (never live in ctest)

```text
max |F_product − F_fd(h=1e-5)| ≤ 1e-6 Ha/Bohr
|sum F| ≤ 1e-8 Ha/Bohr
```

